# Disable clang-tidy entirely for vendored / third-party code.
#
# clang-tidy applies the *nearest* .clang-tidy walking up from each file, so
# this file shadows the repository-root config for everything under 3rdParty/.
# We neither own nor style this code (it is also compiled with -w, warnings
# off, in 3rdParty/CMakeLists.txt), so analyzing it only produces noise.
#
# Note: run-clang-tidy / utils/clang-tidy.sh additionally avoid *invoking*
# clang-tidy on 3rdParty translation units in the first place; this file is the
# backstop for the case where a 3rdParty header is reached transitively.
Checks: '-*'
